{"tool_name":"lipidex","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"lipidex","home":"https://github.com/coongroup/LipiDex","license":"MIT","summary":"A tool for high-confidence LC-MS/MS (Liquid Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry) lipid identification.","addition_date":"2018-08-01T11:58:12Z","last_update_date":"2022-01-11T16:47:20.104435Z","tool_type":["Desktop application","Workbench"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:lipidex","credit":[{"email":"lipidexcontact@gmail.com","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Paul Hutchins","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6683-5735","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/coongroup/LipiDex/wiki"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Natural product identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3803"},{"term":"Peak detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3215"},{"term":"Spectral analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3214"}]}],"name":"LipiDex","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.cels.2018.03.011","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2018 Elsevier Inc.State-of-the-art proteomics software routinely quantifies thousands of peptides per experiment with minimal need for manual validation or processing of data. For the emerging field of discovery lipidomics via liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry (LC-MS/MS), comparably mature informatics tools do not exist. Here, we introduce LipiDex, a freely available software suite that unifies and automates all stages of lipid identification, reducing hands-on processing time from hours to minutes for even the most expansive datasets. LipiDex utilizes flexible in silico fragmentation templates and lipid-optimized MS/MS spectral matching routines to confidently identify and track hundreds of lipid species and unknown compounds from diverse sample matrices. Unique spectral and chromatographic peak purity algorithms accurately quantify co-isolation and co-elution of isobaric lipids, generating identifications that match the structural resolution afforded by the LC-MS/MS experiment. During final data filtering, ionization artifacts are removed to significantly reduce dataset redundancy. LipiDex interfaces with several LC-MS/MS software packages, enabling robust lipid identification to be readily incorporated into pre-existing data workflows. Hutchins et al. introduce an open-source software suite that automates lipid identification and significantly reduces hands-on processing time for large LC-MS/MS lipidomic datasets. They demonstrate the confident identification of hundreds of diverse lipids from complex lipid extracts using optimized spectral matching techniques and multiple identification filters.","authors":[{"name":"Coon J.J."},{"name":"Hutchins P.D."},{"name":"Russell J.D."}],"citationCount":45,"date":"2018-05-23T00:00:00Z","journal":"Cell Systems","title":"LipiDex: An Integrated Software Package for High-Confidence Lipid Identification"},"pmid":"29705063","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Lipids","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0153"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"LipiDex","home":"https://bio.tools/lipidex","license":"MIT","summary":"A tool for high-confidence LC-MS/MS (Liquid Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry) lipid identification.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:lipidex/app/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"